From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: decode PPE egress port and NBQ in debugfs

A BIND entry alone does not prove that a hardware-offloaded flow targets the
physical WAN selected by multi-WAN policy. Decode the FOE IB2 PSE port and NBQ
fields in debugfs so GDM3/GDM4 external-SerDes egress can be verified directly.

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
@@ -125,8 +125,10 @@ static int airoha_ppe_debugfs_foe_show(struct seq_file *m, void *private,
 		seq_printf(m, " eth=%pM->%pM etype=%04x data=%08x"
 			      " vlan=%d,%d ib1=%08x ib2=%08x"
-			      " packets=%llu bytes=%llu\n",
+			      " pse=%u nbq=%u packets=%llu bytes=%llu\n",
 			   h_source, h_dest, l2->etype, data,
 			   l2->vlan1, l2->vlan2, hwe->ib1, ib2,
+			   FIELD_GET(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PSE_PORT, ib2),
+			   FIELD_GET(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_NBQ, ib2),
 			   stats.packets, stats.bytes);
 	}
 
